ng operators and `and`/`or`, changing constants, removing `not`, and replacing statements with `pass`. The first draft of the suite killed 1,042 of them. After three rounds of adding tests for the survivors, it kills 1,108 and 32 survive. Your real mutmut run will make different mutants, so its score won't match this one exactly.\n\n**What the 32 survivors are:**\n- **20 are docstring edits**, which no test can detect.\n- **12 don't change behaviour**, so no test can catch them either. Examples:\n  - The prefix-length check in `int_convert` (`> 2`): any input where the mutant changes the base ends up with the same number.\n  - `ljust(6)` becoming `ljust(7)` before truncating to 6 digits.\n  - The unused `extra_types` parameter of `Parser.findall`.\n  - Wrapping `\"xX\"` or `ALLOWED_TYPES` in extra characters that are already allowed.\n\n**What the tests cover:**\n- Every type code (`d n b o x X % f F e E g G w W s S D l`), including signs, the `0x`/`0b`/`0o` prefixes, `nan`/`inf`, the `.0f` case, and grouping with `,` and `_`.\n- Width, precision, alignment, fill characters (including ones that need regex escaping), and `=` alignment.\n- All date/time types (`ti tg ta te th tc tt ts`), every month name, AM/PM handling and timezone offsets. They're also tested after other fields, because preceding fields change which regex groups the date fields read from.\n- `%`-style date formats.\n- Field names with dots, brackets or hyphens, the collisions between them, and repeated names.\n- `search` and `findall` with `pos`, `endpos`, case sensitivity and `evaluate_result`; `Result`, `Match`, `Parser.__repr__` and exact error messages.\n\n**Two things worth knowing:**\n- The `TooManyFields` error can't happen on Python 3.13, so those tests replace the module's `re` with a stub to reach that code.\n- You'll see two DeprecationWarnings. They come from Python itself when a date format has no year, not from the tests.\n\nI haven't committed anything; `tests/` is still untracked.","